{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.qou_canonical_action","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.qou_canonical_action","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qou_canonical_action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qou_canonical_action","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L36-L110","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\nLet $(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)$ be a\n([quantum observable universe](#def:quantum-observable-universe)) equipped with\nconnection $\\nabla$ ([categorical connection](#def:categorical-connection)),\nsubstrate parameter $q$ ([substrate parameter](#def:substrate-parameter)),\n$q$-Hodge star $\\star_q$ ([$q$-Hodge star](#def:q-hodge-star)),\nand state $\\psi \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to A$.\nThen $(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)$ determines a\n([categorical action](#def:categorical-action)), unique up to a scalar\n$\\lambda \\in R^{\\times}$,\n\n$$\n  \\mathfrak{S}_q\n  = \n  \\mathrm{tr}(\\mathcal{L}_q),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathcal{L}_q = \\mathcal{L}_q(\\nabla, \\psi)$ is the categorical\nLagrangian ([categorical Lagrangian](#def:categorical-lagrangian)).\nThe Lagrangian endomorphism is $\\Phi_q = \\mathcal{L}_q$.\n\nThe square of the Dirac operator\n([categorical Dirac operator](#def:categorical-dirac-operator))\ndecomposes via the Frobenius--Hopf structure as\n\n$$\n  \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla^{2}\n  = \n  q \\cdot R_{\\int} +  \\mathrm{tr}_A\\!\\bigl(\n    F_\\nabla \\wedge_q \\star_q F_\\nabla\n  \\bigr),\n$$\n\nso the categorical action expands to three terms:\n\n```tex\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:canonical-action-decomposition}\n  \\mathfrak{S}_q[\\nabla, \\textstyle\\int_A, \\psi]\n  = \n  \\underbrace{%\n    \\mathrm{tr}\\bigl(q \\cdot R_{\\int}\\bigr)\n  }_{\\text{gravity}}\n  + \n  \\underbrace{%\n    \\int_A \\!\\circ \\mathrm{tr}_A\\bigl(\n      F_\\nabla \\wedge_q \\star_q F_\\nabla\n    \\bigr)\n  }_{\\text{gauge}}\n  + \n  \\underbrace{%\n    \\int_A\\!\\bigl(\\psi^* \\cdot \\mathcal{D}_\\nabla\\psi\\bigr)\n  }_{\\text{matter}},\n\\end{equation}\n```\n\nwith notation as in [categorical action notation](#sec:categorical-action-notation).\nHere $\\mathrm{tr} = \\mathrm{ev}_A \\circ (\\mathrm{id}_{A^\\vee} \\otimes {-}) \\circ \\mathrm{coev}_A$ is the categorical trace, which plays the role of\nspacetime integration; $R_{\\int}$ is the Frobenius--Ricci endomorphism;\nand $F_\\nabla = \\nabla^2$ is the curvature.\n\n*Uniqueness up to scalar.*  The evaluation and coevaluation maps are\ndetermined up to unique isomorphism by \n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below *names* the residual proposition as a\n    `def … : Prop` over the manuscript context — the boxed\n    decomposition `𝒮_q = 𝒮_grav + 𝒮_gauge + 𝒮_matter`.  Naming the\n    conditional conjecture is honest per §3b; an instance discharging\n    it (none here) would be the conjecture, the open state being the\n    absence of one. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:qou-canonical-action","label":"prop:qou-canonical-action","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/qou-canonical-action.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_matter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_matter","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L34-L34","doc":"Matter term `∫ (ψ* · D_∇ ψ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_gauge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_gauge","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L32-L32","doc":"Gauge term `∫ tr(F ∧_q ⋆_q F)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_grav","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_grav","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L30-L30","doc":"Gravity term `tr(q · R_∫)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.S_q","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L28-L28","doc":"The categorical action `𝒮_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.q","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L26-L26","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L24-L24","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QouCanonicalActionContext","kind":"class","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/qou_canonical_action.lean#L18-L34","doc":"Abstract context for the `qou_canonical_action` claim — the\nmanuscript-themed typed fields the claim ranges over.  The\nresidual `Prop` (the boxed three-term decomposition) is *named*\nby `qou_canonical_action` below (§3b: naming a conditional\nconjecture is not a logical claim), not faked by projecting a\n`claim_*` field. ","signatureChunk":0}]}